{
  "title": "23: al-Momenoon المؤمنون",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقَدْ اَفْلَحَ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ‏(1)\nQAD AFLAHA MOAMENOONA.\nIndeed successful are the believers,\nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ فِىْ صَلَاتِهِمْ خَاشِعُوْنَ ۙ‏(2)\nLAZEENA HUM FEE SALAATEHIM KHAASHEU’OONA.\nThose who in their prayers are humble,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَنِ اللَّغْوِ مُعْرِضُوْنَۙ‏(3)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM A’NIL AL-LAGHWE MUA’REZOONA.\nAnd those who, from what is vain, keep (themselves) aloof,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِلزَّكٰوةِ فَاعِلُوْنَۙ‏(4)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM LELZZAKAAWTE FAAE’ELOONA.\nAnd those who act for purification,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِفُرُوْجِهِمْ حٰفِظُوْنَۙ‏(5)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM LEFUROOJEHEM HAAFEZOONA.\nAnd those who guard their private parts,\nاِلَّا عَلٰٓى اَزْوَاجِهِمْ اَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُهُمْ فَاِنَّهُمْ غَيْرُ مَلُوْمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(6)\nILLAA A’LAA AZWAAJEHIM AW MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOHUM FA INNAHUM GHAYRO MALOOMEENA.\nExcept from their wives or those whom their right hands possess for then verily they are not blameable,\nفَمَنِ ابْتَغٰى وَرَآءَ ذٰ لِكَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْعٰدُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(7)\nFAMANE’ ABTAGHAA WARAAA-A ZAA LEKA FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL AL-A’AADOONA.\nBut whosoever seeketh beyond that, then, these are they the transgressors of the bounds,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِاَمٰنٰتِهِمْ وَعَهْدِهِمْ رَاعُوْنَ ۙ‏(8)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM LEAAMAANAATEHEM WAA’AHDEHEM RAAU’OONA.\nAnd those who keep well their trusts and (honour) their promises,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَلٰى صَلَوٰتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُوْنَ‌ۘ‏(9)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM A’LAA SALAWTEHEM YUHAAFEZOONA.\nAnd those who take care of (the regularity in) their prayers,\nاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْوَارِثُوْنَ ۙ‏(10)\nOOLAAA-EKA HOMUL AL-WAARESOONA.\nThese, they are the heirs,\nالَّذِيْنَ يَرِثُوْنَ الْفِرْدَوْسَؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(11)\nLAZEENA YARESOONA AL-FERDAWSA HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\n(These are) those who inherit the Paradise; they shall abide therein.\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ سُلٰلَةٍ مِّنْ طِيْنٍ‌ ۚ‏(12)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL INSAANA MIN SULAALATIN MIN TEENIN.\nAnd indeed We, created man, from an extract of clay,\nثُمَّ جَعَلْنٰهُ نُطْفَةً فِىْ قَرَارٍ مَّكِيْنٍ‏(13)\nSUMMA LAW NUTFATAN FEE QARAARIN MMAKEENIN.\nThen We made him sperm, in a firm resting place,\nثُمَّ خَلَقْنَا النُّطْفَةَ عَلَقَةً فَخَلَقْنَا الْعَلَقَةَ مُضْغَةً فَخَلَقْنَا الْمُضْغَةَ عِظٰمًا فَكَسَوْنَا الْعِظٰمَ لَحْمًا ثُمَّ اَنْشَاْنٰهُ خَلْقًا اٰخَرَ‌ ؕ فَتَبٰرَكَ اللّٰهُ اَحْسَنُ الْخٰلِقِيْنَ ؕ‏(14)\nSUMMA KHALAQNAL AN-NUTFATA A’ALAQATAN FA KHALAQNAL AL-A’ALAQATA MUZGHATAN FA KHALAQNAL AL-MUZGHATA E’EZAAMAN FAKASAWNAA AL-E’EZAAMA SUMMA NAKSOOHAA SUMMA AANSHAANAAHU KHALQAN AAKHAR FA TABAARAKAS-MO LAAHO AHSANO AL-KHAALEQEENA.\nThen made We the sperm a clot, then made We the clot a lump of flesh, then made We in the lump of flesh bones, then clothed We the bones with flesh; then We did grow it into another creation; so Blessed be God, the Best of the creators.\nثُمَّ اِنَّكُمْ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ لَمَيِّتُوْنَؕ‏(15)\nSUMMA INNAKUM BA’DA ZAALEKA LAMAYTOONA.\nThen verily after that ye shall die,\nثُمَّ اِنَّكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ تُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(16)\nSUMMA INNAKUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE TUBA’ASOONA.\nThen verily on the Day of Judgment ye shall be raised.\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا فَوْقَكُمْ سَبْعَ طَرَآئِقَ ۖ  وَمَا كُنَّا عَنِ الْخَلْقِ غٰفِلِيْنَ‏(17)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL FAWQAKUM SAB-A’ TARAAEQA WA MAA KUNNAA A’NIL AL-KHALQE GHAAFELEENA.\nAnd indeed made We above you seven paths (heavens); and neither, of the creation, We are heedless\nوَاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءًۢ بِقَدَرٍ فَاَسْكَنّٰهُ فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ۖ وَاِنَّا عَلٰى ذَهَابٍۢ بِهٖ لَقٰدِرُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(18)\nWA ANZALNAA MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN BEQADARIN FAASKANNAAHU FIL ARZE WA INNAA A’LAA ZAHAABIN BEHI LAQAADEROONA.\nAnd send We down water from the heaven according to a measure, and We cause it to settle in the earth; and verily to take it away We are able.\nفَاَنْشَاْنَا لَكُمْ بِهٖ جَنّٰتٍ مِّنْ نَّخِيْلٍ وَّ اَعْنَابٍ‌ ۘ لَكُمْ فِيْهَا فَوَاكِهُ كَثِيْرَةٌ وَّمِنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ ۙ‏(19)\nFA ANSHAANAA LAKUM BEHI JANNAATIN MIN NAKHEELINW WA AAA’NAABIN LAKUM FEEHAA FAWAAKEHU KASEERATUN WWAMENHAA TAAKULOONA.\nThen with it We grow for you gardens of date-palms and grapes; for you therein are fruits in plenty and from them ye do eat,\nوَشَجَرَةً تَخْرُجُ مِنْ طُوْرِ سَيْنَآءَ تَنْۢبُتُ بِالدُّهْنِ وَصِبْغٍ لِّلْاٰكِلِيْنَ‏(20)\nWASHAJARATAN TAKHROJO MIN TOORE SAYNAAA TANBUTU BEALDDUHNE WASEBGHIN LLELAAAKELEENA.\nAnd a tree that groweth out of Mount Sinai which produceth oil and a condiment for those who eat.\nوَ اِنَّ لَكُمْ فِى الْاَنْعَامِ لَعِبْرَةً‌   ؕ نُسْقِيْكُمْ مِّمَّا فِىْ بُطُوْنِهَا وَلَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَنَافِعُ كَثِيْرَةٌ وَّمِنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ ۙ‏(21)\nWA INNAL LAKUM FIL AL-AANA’AAME LAE’EBRATAN NUSQEEKUM MIMMAA FEE BUTOONEHAA WA LAKUM FEEHAA MANAAFE-O’ KASEERATUN WWAMENHAA TAAKULOONA.\nAnd verily for you there is, in the cattle a lesson; We Provide you to drink of what is in their bellies, and for you there are in them benefits in plenty, and of them ye do eat,\nوَعَلَيْهَا وَعَلَى الْفُلْكِ تُحْمَلُوْنَ‏(22)\nMAKTASABAT RABBANAA WA FULKE TUHMALOONA.\nAnd on them and on ships are ye borne.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ فَقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(23)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ARSALNAA ELAA QAWMEHI FAQAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH AFALAA TATTAQOON.\nAnd indeed sent We Noah unto his people, and he said: “O’ My people! worship ye God (alone) ye have no god other than Him; Will ye not then guard (yourselves against evil)?\nفَقَالَ الْمَلَؤُا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ ۙ يُرِيْدُ اَنْ يَّتَفَضَّلَ عَلَيْكُمْ ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَاَنْزَلَ مَلٰٓئِكَةً  ۖۚ مَّا سَمِعْنَا بِهٰذَا فِىْۤ اٰبَآئِنَا الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‌ ۚ‏(24)\nFAQAALA MALA-O LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QAWMEHI MAA HAAZAA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM YOREEDO AN YYATAFAZZALA A’LAYKUM WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LA-ANZALA MALAAA-EKATAN MAA SAMEA’NAA BEHAAZAA FEE AABAAA-ENAL AWWALEEN.\nBut said the chiefs of those who disbelieved, among from his people: “This is a man like unto yourselves who intendeth to exalt himself above you; but had God will (to send any apostle) He would certainly have sent angels. We have heard not of this among our fathers of old;\nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا رَجُلٌۢ بِهٖ جِنَّةٌ فَتَرَبَّصُوْا بِهٖ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(25)\nIN HOWA ILLAA RAJOLUM BEHI JENNATUN FATARABBASOOA BEHI HATTAA HEEN.\nVerily he is not but a man maniac so bear ye with him for some time.\nقَالَ رَبِّ انْصُرْنِىْ بِمَا كَذَّبُوْنِ‏(26)\nQAALA RABBE SURNEE BEMAA KAZZABOONE.\nHe (Noah) said: “O’ my Lord! help me against what they belie.\nفَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ اَنِ اصْنَعِ الْفُلْكَ بِاَعْيُنِنَا وَ وَحْيِنَا فَاِذَا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا وَفَارَ التَّنُّوْرُ‌ۙ فَاسْلُكْ فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلٍّ زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَاَهْلَكَ اِلَّا مَنْ سَبَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْقَوْلُ مِنْهُمْ‌ۚ وَلَا تُخَاطِبْنِىْ فِى الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا‌ۚ اِنَّهُمْ مُّغْرَقُوْنَ‏(27)\nFAAWHAYNAA ELAYHE SAALEHAN ASNAE’E AL-FULKA BEAAA’YUNENAA WA WAHYENAA FA-EZAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA WAFAARA AT-TANNOORU FAASLUK FEEHAA MIN KULLIN ZAWJAYNE NAYNE WA AHLAKA ILLAA MAN SABAQA A’LAYHE QAWLO MINHUM WA LAA TUKHAATEBNEAA FIL LAZEENA ZALAMOO INNAHUM MUGHRAQOON.\nSo revealed We unto him that: “Make thou (O’ Our Apostle Noah!) the Ark before Our eyes and (as per) Our revelation and when cometh (unto thee) Our command, and gusheth forth water from the oven, take into it two of every species a pair and thy people except those among them about whom had already been issued the word; and address Me not in respect of those who are unjust; for verily they shall be drowned.\nفَاِذَا اسْتَوَيْتَ اَنْتَ وَمَنْ مَّعَكَ عَلَى الْفُلْكِ فَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ نَجّٰٮنَا مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(28)\nFA-EZAA ASTAWAYTA ANTA WA MAN BEMAM A’LAL FULKE FA QOLIL HAMDO LILLAAHE LAZEE NAJJAANAA MENAL QAWMIL ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd when thou art settled (in the Ark), thou and those with thee, then say thou: “All praise be unto God Who delivered us from the unjust people!\nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اَنْزِلْنِىْ مُنْزَلًا مُّبٰرَكًا وَّاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْمُنْزِلِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA QUL RABBIL AANZELNEAA MUNZALAN MMUBAARAKAN WWAANTA KHAYRUR AL-MUNZELEENA.\nAnd say thou: “O’ my Lord! disembark me with a blessed landing, for Thou art the Best of all who cause to land!\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ وَّاِنْ كُنَّا لَمُبْتَلِيْنَ‏(30)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL WA KUNNAA LAMUBTALEENA.\nVerily in this are signs and We do only try (the people).\nثُمَّ اَنْشَاْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ قَرْنًا اٰخَرِيْنَ‌ ۚ‏(31)\nSUMMA ANSHAANAA MIN BA’DEHIM QARNAN AAKHEREEN.\nThen We raised up after them another generation (Hud).\nفَاَرْسَلْنَا فِيْهِمْ رَسُوْلًا مِّنْهُمْ اَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ‌ ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(32)\nFA-ARSALNAA FEEHIM RASOOLAM MINHUM SAALEHAN BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH AFALAA TATTAQOON.\nThen sent We among them an apostle (Saleh) from among themselves saying “Worship ye God (alone), there is not for you any god other than Him: What! Will ye not therefore guard (against evil)?\nوَقَالَ الْمَلَاُ مِنْ قَوْمِهِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَكَذَّبُوْا بِلِقَآءِ الْاٰخِرَةِ وَاَتْرَفْنٰهُمْ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ۙ مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ ۙ يَاْكُلُ مِمَّا تَاْكُلُوْنَ مِنْهُ وَيَشْرَبُ مِمَّا تَشْرَبُوْنَ ۙ‏(33)\nWA QAALA MALA-O MIN QAWMEHE LAZEENA KAFAROO WA KAZZABOO BELEQAAE AAKHERATE WAATRAFNAAHUM FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA MAA HAAZAA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM YAAKULU MIMMAA TAAKULOONA MINHO WAYASHRABU MIMMAA TASHRABOONA.\nAnd the chiefs of his people who disbelieved and belied the meeting of the hereafter, and whom We had richly provided in the life of this world said: “This is not but a man like yourselves, eateth he of what ye eat from, and drinketh he of what ye drink,\nوَلَئِنْ اَطَعْتُمْ بَشَرًا مِّثْلَكُمْ اِنَّكُمْ اِذًا لَّخٰسِرُوْنَۙ‏(34)\nWA LAIN AATAA’TUM BASHARAN MMESLAKUM INNAKUM EZAL LLAKHAASEROONA.\nAnd if ye follow a man like yourselves, verily then ye be the losers.\nاَيَعِدُكُمْ اَنَّكُمْ اِذَا مِتُّمْ وَكُنْتُمْ تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا اَنَّكُمْ مُّخْرَجُوْنَ ۙ‏(35)\nAAYAE’EDUKUM ANNAKUM EZAA METTUM WA KUNTUM TORAABANW WA E’ZAAMAN ANNAKUM MMUKHRAJOONA.\nWhat! doth he promise you that when ye are dead and become dust and bones that ye shall be brought forth?\nهَيْهَاتَ هَيْهَاتَ لِمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ ۙ‏(36)\nHAYHAATA HAYHAATA LEMAKH TOO-A’DOON.\nFar, Far (from sense) is what ye are promised!\nاِنْ هِىَ اِلَّا حَيَاتُنَا الدُّنْيَا نَمُوْتُ وَنَحْيَا وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَبْعُوْثِيْنَ ۙ‏(37)\nIN HEYA ILLAA HAYAATUNAA DUNYAA NAMOOTU WANAHYAA WA MAA NAHNO BEMABU’OOSEENA.\nThere is nothing but our life in this world: We die and we live and we shall not be raised again.\nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا رَجُلُ اۨفْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا وَّمَا نَحْنُ لَهٗ بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(38)\nIN HOWA ILLAA RAJULU TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN WA MAA NAHNO LAHU BE-MOAMENEEN.\nHe is nothing but a man who hath forged a lie about God, and we are not going to believe in him.\nقَالَ رَبِّ انْصُرْنِىْ بِمَا كَذَّبُوْنِ‏(39)\nQAALA RABBE SURNEE BEMAA KAZZABOONE.\nHe (Saleh) said: “O’ my Lord! help me against what they belie!\nقَالَ عَمَّا قَلِيْلٍ لَّيُصْبِحُنَّ نٰدِمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(40)\nQAALA A’MMAA QALEELIN LLAYUSBEHUNNA NAADEMEENA.\nSaid (God): “Yet a while, they will soon turn repentant,\nفَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّيْحَةُ بِالْحَقِّ فَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ غُثَآءً‌ۚ فَبُعْدًا لِّلْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(41)\nFA-AKHAZATHOMUR AS-SAYHATU BIL-HAQQE FAJAA’ALNAAHUM GHOSAAA-AN FABUA’DAN LLELQAWME ZAALEMEEN.\nThen did the (awful) cry, in truth overtook them, and We made them like a rubbish; so away with the unjust people!\nثُمَّ اَنْشَاْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ قُرُوْنًا اٰخَرِيْنَؕ‏(42)\nSUMMA ANSHAANAA MIN BA’DEHIM QOROONAN AAAKHAREENA.\nThen We raised after them other generations.\nمَا تَسْبِقُ مِنْ اُمَّةٍ اَجَلَهَا وَمَا يَسْتَاْخِرُوْنَؕ‏(43)\nMAA TASBEQU MIN UMMATIN AAJALAHAA WA MAA YASTAAKHEROONA.\nNo people can hasten their (fixed) term, nor can they delay (it).\nثُمَّ اَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلَنَا تَتْرَا‌ ؕ كُلَّ مَا جَآءَ اُمَّةً رَّسُوْلُهَا كَذَّبُوْهُ‌ فَاَتْبَعْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ بَعْضًا وَّجَعَلْنٰهُمْ اَحَادِيْثَ‌ ۚ فَبُعْدًا لِّقَوْمٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(44)\nSUMMA ARSALNAA RUSULANAA TATRAA KULLA MAA JAAA-A UMMATAM RRASOOLUHAA KAZZABOOHU FAATBAA’NAA BA’ZAHUM BA’ZAN WWAJAA’ALNAAHUM AAHAADEESA FABUA’DAN LEQAWMINY LAA YOAMENOONA.\nThen sent We Our apostles one after another; whenever came unto a people their apostle, they belied him, so caused We some to follow the others and made (of) some stories (of old), so away with the people who believe not.\nثُمَّ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى وَاَخَاهُ هٰرُوْنَ ۙ بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(45)\nSUMMA ARSALNAA MOOSAA WAAKHAAHU AALO BE-AAYAATENAA WASULTAANIN MOBEEN.\nThen sent We Moses and his brother, Aaron, with Our signs and a manifest authority,\nاِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ئِهٖ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا وَكَانُوْا قَوْمًا عٰلِيْنَ‌ ۚ‏(46)\nELAA FIR-A’WNA WAMALAAEH FAS-TAKBAROO WA KAANOO QAWMAN A’AALEENA.\nUnto Pharaoh and his chiefs, but they behaved proudly and they were a haughty people.\nفَقَالُوْۤا اَنُؤْمِنُ لِبَشَرَيْنِ مِثْلِنَا وَقَوْمُهُمَا لَنَا عٰبِدُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(47)\nFA-QAALOO A-NOAMENO LEBASHARAYNE MESLENAA WAQAWMUHUMAA LANAA A’ABEDOON.\nAnd said they: “What! Shall we believe in two men like ourselves whose people are unto us servile.\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُمَا فَكَانُوْا مِنَ الْمُهْلَكِيْنَ‏(48)\nFA-KAZZABOOHOMAA FA KAANOO MENAL AL-MUHLAKEENA.\nSo they did belie them, so became they of those destroyed.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(49)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA LA-A’LLAHUM YAHTADOON.\nAnd indeed We gave Moses the Book happly they may be guided aright.\nوَجَعَلْنَا ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ وَاُمَّهٗۤ اٰيَةً وَّاٰوَيْنٰهُمَاۤ اِلٰى رَبْوَةٍ ذَاتِ قَرَارٍ وَّمَعِيْنٍ‏(50)\nWA JA-A’LNAA NA MARYAMAL WAAMMAH AAYATAL WWAAWAYNAAHUMAA ELAA RABWATIN ZAATIL QARAARIN WWAMAE’EENIN.\nAnd made We the Son of Mary and his Mother a Sign, and We gave them a refuge for both on a high land, quiet, secure and watered with springs\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الرُّسُلُ كُلُوْا مِنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ وَاعْمَلُوْا صَالِحًا‌ ؕ اِنِّىْ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ عَلِيْمٌ ؕ‏(51)\nYAA AYYOHAL ROSOLO KOLOO MENAL AT-TAYBAATE WAAA’MALOOA SAALEHAN INNEE BEMAA TA’MALOON A’LEEM.\n(And the apostles were commanded by God) “O’ (My) apostles! eat ye of the good things and do good; Verily I know what ye do.\nوَاِنَّ هٰذِهٖۤ اُمَّتُكُمْ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّاَنَا رَبُّكُمْ فَاتَّقُوْنِ‏(52)\nWA INNA HAAZEHI AUMMATUKUM UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN WWAANAA RABBOKUM FAT-TAQOON.\nAnd verily this your group is one group, and I am your Lord therefore fear ye (Only Me).\nفَتَقَطَّعُوْۤا اَمْرَهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ زُبُرًا‌ ؕ كُلُّ حِزْبٍۢ بِمَا لَدَيْهِمْ فَرِحُوْنَ‏(53)\nFATAQATTAU’OOA AAMRAHUM BAYNAHUM ZUBURAN KULLO HIZBIM BEMAA LADAYHIM FAREEHOON.\nBut they have rent the unity among themselves into sects; each party rejoiceth in that which is with them.\nفَذَرْهُمْ فِىْ غَمْرَتِهِمْ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(54)\nFAZARHUM FEE GHAMRATEHEM HATTAA HEEN.\nSo leave them in their over whelming ignorance till a certain time.\nاَيَحْسَبُوْنَ اَنَّمَا نُمِدُّهُمْ بِهٖ مِنْ مَّالٍ وَّبَنِيْنَۙ‏(55)\nAAYAHSABOONA ANNAMAA NUMEDDUHUM BEHI MIN MMAALIN WWABANEENA.\nWhat! Think they that what We aid them with of wealth and children,\nنُسَارِعُ لَهُمْ فِى الْخَيْرٰتِ‌ ؕ بَلْ لَّا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(56)\nNUSAAREU’U LAHUM FIL AL-KHAYRAATE BAL LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nWe are hastening unto them the good things? Nay! they (only) perceive not.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ هُمْ مِّنْ خَشْيَةِ رَبِّهِمْ مُّشْفِقُوْنَۙ‏(57)\nINNAL LAZEENA HUM MIN KHASYATIL RABBEHIM MMUSHFEQOONA.\nAnd Verily they who are thrilled for fear of their Lord,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ يُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ‏(58)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHIM YOAMENOONA.\nAnd those who believe in the signs of their Lord,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِرَبِّهِمْ لَا يُشْرِكُوْنَۙ‏(59)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM BE-RABBEHIM LAA YUSHREKOON.\nAnd those who associate not (anything) with their Lord,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُؤْتُوْنَ مَاۤ اٰتَوْا وَّ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَجِلَةٌ اَنَّهُمْ اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْ رٰجِعُوْنَ ۙ‏(60)\nWAL LAZEENA YOATOONAZ MAA AAATAWA WA QULOOBUHUM WAJELATUN ANNAHUM ELAA RABBEHIM RAAJE-O’ON.\nAnd those who give what they give (in charity) while their hearts thrilled for fear that unto their Lord they must return,\nاُولٰٓئِكَ يُسَارِعُوْنَ فِىْ الْخَيْرٰتِ وَهُمْ لَهَا سٰبِقُوْنَ‏(61)\nOOLAAA-EKA YUSAAREU’OONA FEE AL-KHAYRAATE WA HUM LAHAA SAABEQOONA.\nThese (are they who) hasten unto good things and they are the foremost to (attain) them,\nوَلَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفْسًا اِلَّا وُسْعَهَا‌ وَلَدَيْنَا كِتٰبٌ يَّنْطِقُ بِالْحَقِّ‌ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA LAA NUKALLEFU NAFSAN ILLAA WUS-A’HAA WA LADAYNAA KETAABUM YYANTEQU BIL-HAQQE WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nAnd task We not a soul but to the extent of its ability and with Us is a Book, it speaketh the truth, and they shall not be dealt with unjustly.\nبَلْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ فِىْ غَمْرَةٍ مِّنْ هٰذَا وَلَهُمْ اَعْمَالٌ مِّنْ دُوْنِ ذٰلِكَ هُمْ لَهَا عٰمِلُوْنَ‏(63)\nBAL QULOOBUHUM FEE GHAMRATIN MIN HAAZAA WA LAHUM AAA’MAALUN MIN DOONIL ZAALEKA HUM LAHAA A’AMELOON.\nNay! their hearts are in overwhelming ignorance about this, and they have other than this, deeds which they do,\nحَتّٰۤى اِذَاۤ اَخَذْنَا مُتْرَفِيْهِمْ بِالْعَذَابِ اِذَا هُمْ يَجْئَرُوْنَؕ‏(64)\nHATTAA EZAA AKHAZNAA MUTRAFEEHEM BE-A’ZAABE EZAA HUM YAJAROONA.\nUntil seized We the luxurious ones of them with chastisement, Behold! cry they in supplication!\nلَا تَجْئَرُوا الْيَوْمَ‌ اِنَّكُمْ مِّنَّا لَا تُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(65)\nLAA TAJAROOA YAWMA INNAKUM MINNAA LAA TUNSAROONA.\n(It will be said unto them) “Cry not this day for succour! Verily from Us ye shall not be helped!\nقَدْ كَانَتْ اٰيٰتِىْ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فَكُنْتُمْ عَلٰٓى اَعْقَابِكُمْ تَنْكِصُوْنَۙ‏(66)\nQAD KAANAT AAAYAATEAA TUTLAA A’LAYKUM FA KUNTUM A’LAA AAA’QAABEKUM TANKESOONA.\nIndeed My signs were recited unto you, but ye used to turn back on your heels,\nمُسْتَكْبِرِيْنَ ‌ۖ  بِهٖ سٰمِرًا تَهْجُرُوْنَ‏(67)\nMUSTAKBEREENA BEHI SAAMERAN TAHJUROONA.\nPuffed up with pride about it (Qur’an) discoursing foolishly by night.\nاَفَلَمْ يَدَّبَّرُوا الْقَوْلَ اَمْ جَآءَهُمْ مَّا لَمْ يَاْتِ اٰبَآءَهُمُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(68)\nA-FALAM YADDABBAROOA QAWLA AM JAAA-AHUM MAA LAM TAKOONOO AAABAAAHUMU AWWALEEN.\nWhat! Ponder they not over the Word (Qur’an) or hath that come unto them which came not unto their fathers of old?\nاَمْ لَمْ يَعْرِفُوْا رَسُوْلَهُمْ فَهُمْ لَهٗ مُنْكِرُوْنَ‏(69)\nAM LAM YAA’REFOOA RASOOLAHUM FAHUM LAHU MUNKEROONA.\nOr recognize they not their Apostle that they deny him?\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ بِهٖ جِنَّةٌ  ؕ بَلْ جَآءَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَاَكْثَرُهُمْ لِلْحَقِّ كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(70)\nAM YAQOOLOONA BEHI JENNATUN BAL JAAA-AHUM BIL-HAQQE WA AKSAROHUM LIL-HAQQE KAAREHOONA.\nOr say they that there is mania in him? Nay! he hath brought unto them the Truth, but most of them hate the Truth.\nوَلَوِ اتَّبَعَ الْحَقُّ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ لَفَسَدَتِ السَّمٰوٰتُ وَالْاَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِيْهِنَّ‌ؕ بَلْ اَتَيْنٰهُمْ بِذِكْرِهِمْ فَهُمْ عَنْ ذِكْرِهِمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَؕ‏(71)\nWALAWE TABA-A’L HAQQO AHWAAA-AHUM LAFASADATE AS-SAMAAWAATU WAL WA MAN FEEHENNA BAL AATAYNAAHUM BEZEKREHEM FAHUM A’N ZEKREHEM MMUA’REZOONA.\nAnd should the Truth follow their vain inclinations certainly will perish the heavens and the earth and all those who are therein: Nay! he hath brought unto them their Reminder, but from their Reminder they turn aside.\nاَمْ تَسْئَلُهُمْ خَرْجًا فَخَرٰجُ رَبِّكَ خَيْرٌ‌ ‌ۖ  وَّهُوَ خَيْرُ الرّٰزِقِيْنَ‏(72)\nAM TASALUHUM KHARJAN FAKHARAAJU RABBEKA KHAYRUL WA KHAYRUR RAAZEQEEN.\nOr is it that thou asketh them for a tribute? But the recompense of thy Lord is the Best; and He is the Best of the sustainers.\nوَاِنَّكَ لَتَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(73)\nWA LATADU’OOHUM ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nAnd verily thou callest them unto the straight path;\nوَاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ عَنِ الصِّرَاطِ لَنٰكِبُوْنَ‏(74)\nWA INNA LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE A’NIL AS-SERAATE LANAAKEBOONA.\nAnd verily those who believe not in the hereafter are from the (right) path, the deviators\nوَلَوْ رَحِمْنٰهُمْ وَكَشَفْنَا مَا بِهِمْ مِّنْ ضُرٍّ لَّلَجُّوْا فِىْ طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(75)\nWA LAW RAHEMNAAHUM WAKASHAFNAA MAA BEHIM MIN ZURRIN LLALAJJOOA FEE TUGHYAANEHIM YA’MAHOON.\nAnd should We have mercy on them and (should) We relieve (them) of their distress, they would obstinately persist in their transgression, blindly wandering on.\nوَلَقَدْ اَخَذْنٰهُمْ بِالْعَذَابِ فَمَا اسْتَكَانُوْا لِرَبِّهِمْ وَمَا يَتَضَرَّعُوْنَ‏(76)\nWA LAQAD AAKHAZNAAHUM BE-A’ZAABE FAMAA ASTAKAANOOA LE-RABBEHIM WA MAA YATAZARRAU’OONA.\nAnd indeed We seized them with a chastisement but they sub mitted not themselves unto their Lord, nor did they humble themselves (unto Him).\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا فَتَحْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ بَابًا ذَا عَذَابٍ شَدِيْدٍ اِذَا هُمْ فِيْهِ مُبْلِسُوْنَ‏(77)\nHATTAA EZAA FATAHNA A’LAYHIM BAABAN ZAL A’ZAABIN BAA-SIN EZAA HUM FEEHE MUBLESOONA.\nUntil when We did open upon them a door of severe chastisement, lo! they got into despair at it.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْشَاَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصَارَ وَالْاَفْئِدَةَ‌  ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(78)\nWA HOWA LAZEE AANSHAA LAKOMUL JA-A’LA LAKOMUS SAM-A’ WA ABSAARA WAL QALEELAA MAA TASHKOROON.\nHe it is Who caused for you the hearing and the sight and hearts; (very) little it is what ye give thanks (unto Him).\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ ذَرَاَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَاِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(79)\nWA HOWA LAZEE ZARA-AKUM FIL ARZE WA ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nHe it is Who multiplied you in the earth, and unto Him (only) ye shall be gathered.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُ وَلَهُ اخْتِلَافُ الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(80)\nWA HOWA LAZEE YOHYEE WA YOMEETO LAHUL AKHTELAAFU LAYLE WA WA AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nAnd He it is Who giveth life and (causeth) death, and (in) His (control) is the alternation of the night and the day; What! do ye not then understand?\nبَلْ قَالُوْا مِثْلَ مَا قَالَ الْاَوَّلُوْنَ‏(81)\nBAL QAALOO MISLA MAA QAALA AWWALOON.\nNay! say they the like of what said the ancients.\nقَالُوْۤا ءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّ عِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَ‏(82)\nQAALOO A-EZAA MITNAA KUNNAA TORAABANW WA E’EZAAMAN A-INNAA LA-MABO’OSOON.\nThey say: “What! When we are dead and become dust and bones, shall we (even) then be raised?\nلَقَدْ وُعِدْنَا نَحْنُ وَاٰبَآؤُنَا هٰذَا مِنْ قَبْلُ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(83)\nLAQAD WO-I’DNAA NAHNO WA AABAAA-ONAA HAAZAA MIN QABLO IN HAAZAA ILLAA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nCertainly this have we been promised, we and (also) our fathers aforetime, but this is not but fables of the ancients.\nقُلْ لِّمَنِ الْاَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِيْهَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(84)\nQUL LLEMANE ARZO WA MAN FEEHAA IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Whose is the earth; whoever is in it, if ye know?\nسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ قُلْ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(85)\nSA-YAQOOLOONA LIL-LAAH QUL AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nThey will say: “God’s,” Say “Will thou (then): “Will ye not reflect?\nقُلْ مَنْ رَّبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ السَّبْعِ وَرَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(86)\nQUL MAN RRABBU SAMAAWAATE AS-SABE’E WA RABBO A’RSHIL A’ZEEM.\nSay thou: “Who is the Lord of the seven heavens, and the Glorious Throne?\nسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ قُلْ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(87)\nSA-YAQOOLOONA LIL-LAAH QUL AFALAA TATTAQOON.\nThey will say: (that they are) “God’s”; (then) Say thou: “Will ye not then guard (yourselves against evil)?\nقُلْ مَنْۢ بِيَدِهٖ مَلَكُوْتُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّهُوَ يُجِيْرُ وَلَا يُجَارُ عَلَيْهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(88)\nQUL MAN BE-YADEHI MALAKOOTO KULLE SHAY-IN WA YUJEERU WA LAA YUJAARU A’LAYHE IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nSay thou: “Who is it in Whose hand is the kingdom of all things and Who protecteth and is never protected? if ye do but know?\nسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ قُلْ فَاَنّٰى تُسْحَرُوْنَ‏(89)\nSA-YAQOOLOONA LIL-LAAH QUL FA-ANNAA TUSHAROONA.\nThey will say: “In God’s” (hand) (then) Say thou: “From whence (then) are ye beguiled?\nبَلْ اَتَيْنٰهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(90)\nBAL AATAYNAAHUM BIL-HAQQE WA INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nNay! We have brought unto them the Truth, and verily they are liars.\nمَا اتَّخَذَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ وَّلَدٍ وَّمَا كَانَ مَعَهٗ مِنْ اِلٰهٍ‌ اِذًا لَّذَهَبَ كُلُّ اِلٰهٍۢ بِمَا خَلَقَ وَلَعَلَا بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ‌ؕ سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَۙ‏(91)\nMAA TAKHAZA LAAHO MIN WWALADIN WA MAA KAANA MA-A’HU MIN ELAAHIN EZAL LLAZAHABA KULLO ELAAHIN BEMAA KHALAQAL WALAA’ALAA KHALAA A’LAA BA’Z WA LAAHE LAAHE A’MMAA YASEFOONA.\nNever did God take unto Him a son and never was there with Him any god - else would each god have certainly taken away what he had created, and some of them would certainly have overpowered others; Far from the glory of God, be what they attribute (unto Him),\nعٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ فَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(92)\nA’ALEMIL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE FATAA’AALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\n(He is) the Knower (alike) of the seen and the unseen, so exalted is He, far above what they join (with Him).\nقُل رَّبِّ اِمَّا تُرِيَنِّىْ مَا يُوْعَدُوْنَۙ‏(93)\nQUL RABBIL IMMAA TUREENNEAA MAA YOOA’ADOONA.\nSay thou: “O’ my Lord! If thou wilt make me see what (chastisement) they are promised,\nرَبِّ فَلَا تَجْعَلْنِىْ فِى الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(94)\nRABBE FALAA TAJA’ALNEAA FIL QAWMIL ZAALEMEEN.\nO’ my Lord! then place me not amidst the unjust people!\nوَاِنَّا عَلٰٓى اَنْ نُّرِيَكَ مَا نَعِدُهُمْ لَقٰدِرُوْنَ‏(95)\nWA INNAA A’LAA AN NNUREEKA MAA NAE’EDUHUM LAQAADEROONA.\nVerily, We are well able to make thee see (the chastisement) what We have promised them.\nاِدْفَعْ بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُ السَّيِّئَةَ‌ ؕ نَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَصِفُوْنَ‏(96)\nBILLATEE BIL-LATEE HEYA AHSANO SAYYEATE NAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YASEFOONA.\nRepel evil by what is best; We know best what they attribute (against thee).\nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ هَمَزٰتِ الشَّيٰطِيْنِۙ‏(97)\nWA QUL RABBIL A-OO’ZO BEKA MIN HAMAZAATE ASH-SHAYTEENE.\nAnd say thou: “O’ my Lord! I seek refuge unto Thee from the (evil) promptings of the satans!\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِكَ رَبِّ اَنْ يَّحْضُرُوْنِ‏(98)\nWA A-OO’ZO BEKA RABBE AN YYAHZUROONE.\nI seek refuge unto Thee O’ my Lord! from their access to me\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءَ اَحَدَهُمُ الْمَوْتُ قَالَ رَبِّ ارْجِعُوْنِۙ‏(99)\nHATTAA EZAA JAAA-A AAHADAHUMU MAWTO QAALA RABBE ARJEU’OONE.\nUntil, when cometh death unto one of them, sayeth he: “My Lord! send me back again (into the world)”,\nلَعَلِّىْۤ اَعْمَلُ صَالِحًا فِيْمَا تَرَكْتُ‌ؕ كَلَّا‌ ؕ اِنَّهَا كَلِمَةٌ هُوَ قَآئِلُهَا‌ؕ وَمِنْ وَّرَآئِهِمْ بَرْزَخٌ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(100)\nLAA’ALLEAA AAA’MALU SAALEHAN FEEMAA TARAKTU KALLAA INNAHAA KALEMATUN HOWA QAAELUHAA WA MIN WA-RAAA-EHIM BARZAKHUL ELAA YAWMIL YUB-A’SOON.\nThat I may do (the) good which I have left undone.” By no means! it is but a word he sayeth; and after them shall be a barrier until the day they shall be raised (again).\nفَاِذَا نُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ فَلَاۤ اَنْسَابَ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ وَّلَا يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(101)\nFA-EZAA NUFEKHA FIL SOORE FALAA AANSAABA BAYNAHUM YAWMA-EZIN WA LAA YATASAAA-ALOON.\nAnd when the trumpet is blown, there shall be no ties of kindred between them on that day, nor shall they ask of one another.\nفَمَنْ ثَقُلَتْ مَوَازِيْنُهٗ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(102)\nFAMAN SAQOLAT MAWAAZEENOHU FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nThen (those) whose scales (of good deeds) are heavy, they shall be the successful ones;\nوَمَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَازِيْنُهٗ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(103)\nWA MAN KHAFFAT MAWAAZEENOHU FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM FEE JAHANNAMA KHAALEDOON.\nAnd those whose scales (of good deeds) are light, they are those who shall lose their souls, abiding in Hell.\nتَلْفَحُ وُجُوْهَهُمُ النَّارُ وَهُمْ فِيْهَا كٰلِحُوْنَ‏(104)\nTALFAHU WUJOOHAHUMU TAMASSANAN WA HUM FEEHAA KAALEHOONA.\nThe fire shall scorch their faces and they therein shall be grinning (of the affliction).\nاَلَمْ تَكُنْ اٰيٰتِىْ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فَكُنْتُمْ بِهَا تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(105)\nALAM TAKUN AAAYAATEAA TUTLAA A’LAYKUM FA KUNTUM BEHAA TOKAZZEBOON.\n(Then will God ask them) “Were not My signs rehearsed unto you? then ye used to belie them\nقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا غَلَبَتْ عَلَيْنَا شِقْوَتُنَا وَكُنَّا قَوْمًا ضَآلِّيْنَ‏(106)\nQAALOO RABBANAA GHALABAT A’LAYNAA SHEQWATUNAA KUNNAA QAWMAN ZAALLEENA.\nThey shall say: “O’ Our Lord! overcame us our ill-luck and we were people gone astray\nرَبَّنَاۤ اَخْرِجْنَا مِنْهَا فَاِنْ عُدْنَا فَاِنَّا ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(107)\nRABBANAA AAKHREJNAA MINHAA FA-IN U’UDNAA FAINNAA ZAALEMOON.\nO’ our Lord! Take us out of it; if we return (to evil) then verily we shall be unjust,\nقَالَ اخْسَئُوْا فِيْهَا وَلَا تُكَلِّمُوْنِ‏(108)\nQAALA AKHSAOOA FEEHAA WA LAA TUKALLEMOONE.\n(God will) say: “Be ye driven down into it, and speak ye not unto Me!\nاِنَّهٗ كَانَ فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْ عِبَادِىْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَاۤ اٰمَنَّا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‌‌ۖ‌ۚ‏(109)\nINNAHU KAANA FAREEQUM MIN E’BAADEE YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA AAMANNAA FAGH-FIR LANAA HAMNAA WA ANTA KHAYRUR AR-RAAHEMEENA.\nVerily, there was a party of My servants who said: “O’ our Lord! we believe, so forgive us and have mercy on us, and Thou art the Best of the Merciful ones!\nفَاتَّخَذْتُمُوْهُمْ سِخْرِيًّا حَتّٰٓى اَنْسَوْكُمْ ذِكْرِىْ وَكُنْتُمْ مِّنْهُمْ تَضْحَكُوْنَ‏(110)\nFAATTAKHAZTUMOOHUM SEKHREEA HATTAA AANSAWKUM ZEKREAA WA KUNTUM MINHUM TAZHAKOONA.\nBut ye took them with ridicule that (until they) made you to neglect My remembrance, while ye did laugh at them.\nاِنِّىْ جَزَيْتُهُمُ الْيَوْمَ بِمَا صَبَرُوْۤا ۙ اَنَّهُمْ هُمُ الْفَآئِزُوْنَ‏(111)\nINNEE JAZAYTUHUMU YAWMA BEMAA SABAROO ANNAHUM HOMUL FAAA-EZOON.\nVerily, I have recompensed them this day for they were patient; (that), they are the achievers.\nقٰلَ كَمْ لَبِثْتُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ عَدَدَ سِنِيْنَ‏(112)\nQAALA KAM LABISTUM FIL ARZE A’ADADA SENEEN.\nHe will say: “How many years did ye tarry in the earth?\nقَالُوْا لَبِثْنَا يَوْمًا اَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ فَسْئَلِ الْعَآدِّيْنَ‏(113)\nQAALOO LABESNAA YAWMAN AW YAWM YAWMIN FASALE AL-A’AADDEENA.\nThey will say: “Tarried we a day or part of a day, ask thou those who keep account\nقٰلَ اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا لَّوْ اَنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(114)\nQAALA IN LLABESTUM ILLAA QALEELAA LAW ANNAKUM KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\n(God will) say: “You did tarry but a little if ye only knew (it)\nاَفَحَسِبْتُمْ اَنَّمَا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ عَبَثًا وَّاَنَّكُمْ اِلَيْنَا لَا تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(115)\nAFAHASIBTUM ANNAMAA KHALAQNAAKUM A’BASANW WA ANNAKUM ELAYNAA LAA TURJAO’ON.\nWhat! think ye then that We created you in vain and that unto Us ye shall not be returned?\nفَتَعٰلَى اللّٰهُ الْمَلِكُ الْحَقُّ‌ ۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ۚ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْكَرِيْمِ‏(116)\nFA-TAA’ALAL LAAHUL MALEKUL HAQQO, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA RABBUL A’RSHIL KAREEM.\nThen (behold) the most exalted is God, the True King; No god is there but He, the Lord of ‘Arsh’ (the Throne) of Grace.\nوَمَنْ يَّدْعُ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَۙ لَا بُرْهَانَ لَهٗ بِهٖۙ فَاِنَّمَا حِسَابُهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(117)\nWA MANY YAD-O’ MA-A’LLAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHARA, LAA BURHAANA LAHU BEHI, FA-INNAMAA HESAABOHU I’NDA RABBEHI, INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUL KAAFEROON.\nAnd whoever invoketh with God another god - he hath no proof therefore - his reckoning is only with his Lord; Verily, the disbelievers shall not be successful.\nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اغْفِرْ وَارْحَمْ وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‏(118)\nWA QUR RABBIGH FIR WAR HAM WA ANTA KHAYRUR RAAHEMEEN.\nAnd say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “O’ my Lord! For give and have mercy, and Thou art the Best of the merciful ones!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Momenoon (The Believers)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 118 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reciter of this Surah will feel great comfort when the angel of death comes to take his soul and he will be given the good news of his position by angels.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites this Surah on every Friday, he will have a great status in the hereafter and will be in the company of prophets. If this Surah is written (at night) and put on the neck of a drunkard, he will start hating intoxicating drinks and will stop this bad habit."
